SITE     name="Tide Mill"  nav="Bread,Visit,Contact"  location="Bristol"  contact="hello@tidemill.co"
THEME    family=editorial  accent=#b8442f  mode=light  density=roomy
SECTION  id=s1  kind=hero  layout=split  tone=quiet
TEXT     sec=s1  slot=eyebrow  text="Bread [worth the walk]"
TEXT     sec=s1  slot=title    text="Two ovens and no cafe."
TEXT     sec=s1  slot=lede     text="We bake sourdough in Bristol, selling out by noon. Visit us before lunch to grab a loaf."
ACTION   sec=s1  slot=primary label="Collection times" href="#times"
ACTION   sec=s1  slot=secondary label="Weekly loaves" href="#loaves"
MEDIA    sec=s1  slot=figure motif=elevation
SECTION  id=s2  kind=features  layout=list  tone=quiet
TEXT     sec=s2  slot=eyebrow  text="The craft"
TEXT     secc=s2  slot=title    text="Sourdough in two ovens."
ITEM      sec=s2  slot=item   title="Fermentation" body="We let the dough rise for twenty-four hours, then score it by hand before baking. The starter is fed twice daily to keep it active and tangy."
ITEM      sec=s2  slot=item   title="Baking stone" body="Each loaf rests on a heated slab that retains heat evenly through the crust's thickness. We rotate stones every morning so no single spot gets too hot or cold during the bake cycle."
ITEM      sec=s2  slot=item   title="Loaf count" body="We start with one hundred grams of flour per kilogram of water, then add salt and yeast to reach a final weight that fits our two ovens. Only forty loaves are baked each day because we cannot keep them fresh longer than six hours."
ITEM      sec=s2  slot=item   title="Cooling rack" body="After the oven door opens, every loaf sits on an elevated grid until it cools completely before being wrapped in linen. This step prevents condensation from making the crust soggy or softening too quickly while still warm."
SECTION  id=s3  kind=roster  layout=stack  tone=quiet
TEXT     sec=s3  slot=eyebrow  text="Meet our bakers"
TEXT     sec=s3  slot=title    text="The hands behind the dough."
ITEM      sec=s3  slot=item   title="Head baker" body="She manages the fermentation schedule and oversees scoring every loaf. Her experience ensures consistency across both ovens while adapting recipes for seasonal flour changes."
ITEM      sec=s3  slot=item   title="Pastry assistant" body="He handles mixing, shaping, and cooling logistics. His focus on timing keeps loaves at peak texture from oven to wrap without overworking the gluten structure during handling."
ITEM      sec=s3  slot=item   title="Quality control" body="They inspect crust colour and internal crumb density before packaging. Their checks ensure every loaf meets our standard for tangy acidity and even bake throughout its thickness."
SECTION  id=s4  kind=detail  layout=split  tone=quiet
TEXT     sec=s4  slot=eyebrow  text="The secret"
TEXT     sec=s4  slot=title    text="Our [starter] lives in a jar."
TEXT     sec=s4  slot=lede  text="Unlike commercial yeast, our wild culture is fed only with flour and water from local wells. It has been active for over two decades, developing a unique acidity that no other baker can replicate without the same living history behind it."
ACTION   sec=s4  slot=primary label="Ask about your starter" href="#starter"
MEDIA    sec=s4  slot=figure motif=elevation
SECTION  id=s5  kind=faq  layout=stack  tone=quiet
TEXT     sec=s5  slot=eyebrow text="Common questions"
TEXT     sec=s5  slot=title    text="What you need to know before visiting."
ITEM      sec=s5  slot=item   title="Do I have a ticket?" body="You must book your collection time online at least two days in advance. Tickets are released daily at midnight and sell out within an hour, so we recommend setting multiple reminders on different devices if possible."
ITEM      sec=s5  slot=item   title="What happens when tickets run out?" body="If all available slots for the day have been taken by noon, you will be placed on a waiting list that is only called back at one o'clock. This means your loaf may arrive slightly later than usual and could miss its peak freshness window."
ITEM      sec=s5  slot=item   title="Can I pick up without booking?" body="No, Tide Mill does not accept walk-ins or last-minute requests due to strict hygiene protocols during the baking cycle. Every customer must present their digital ticket at the door before entering the collection area."
ITEM      sec=s5  slot=item   title="What if my time is cancelled?" body="If you cannot make your scheduled pickup, please contact us by email no later than six hours prior to your appointment so we can reassign that slot or refund it in full within forty-eight hours."
ITEM      sec=s5  slot=item   title="How long does the bread last after I pick it up?" body="Each loaf is baked and cooled at a specific time, then wrapped immediately. You should consume it within two days for optimal texture, though it remains safe to eat if stored in an airtight container for up to five days."
SECTION  id=s6  kind=cta  layout=stack  tone=quiet
TEXT     sec=s6  slot=title    text="Come before lunch."
TEXT     sec=s6  slot=lede     text="The first loaf of every week arrives at nine o'clock sharp; by noon the counter is empty and our doors close for the day. Bring your ticket, bring a bag, come while we still have room to serve you."
ACTION   sec=s6  slot=primary label="Book now" href="#book"
